Six of the seven passed every automated rule. Claude Opus 5.5 Medium was the best overall and fast, about 33 seconds against about 200 for most Gemini runs (they ran concurrently, so some of that is contention). Gemini 3.8 Flash High tied on looks but was slow. GPT-OSS-120B failed: a 503 "no capacity", then a nonsense drawing.

Honestly, at 14 pixels all the checkboxes read slightly octagonal, and the rules did not separate the good ones from the merely passing. I still had to look.

I also ran route C on two models for the title bar buttons (close, zoom and collapse). Opus drew them cleanly. Gemini's plus sign sits off-centre, and both models' × marks have a heavy centre at 12 pixels.

