## The best result: claude-pxl

[claude-pxl](https://github.com/crsolver/claude-pxl) (MIT) is an Agent Skill for "pixel art as code". The model writes a `.px.js` file containing a palette and text grids or shape operations, and the skill builds PNGs, enlarged previews and an ASCII dump you can check by eye. It is route B with proper tooling around it.

The PNGs come out at exactly the size in the file, with alpha strictly 0 or 255 (what a 1-bit mask needs). A build takes about 0.1 seconds, with no dependencies beyond Node.

It is packaged as a Claude skill, but I gave `agy` its `SKILL.md` and reference docs as plain context, and Gemini wrote all eight Halcyon control sprites in one go. Every one of them round-tripped exactly through Scriptoscope's encoder and the runtime decoder.

